<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Tarred_Thoughts.xml               UtinniPatches — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1

  The mood half of item spec §2. Situational (ThoughtWorker_Hediff), not a
  memory — a tarred colonist's mood should track how tarred they currently
  ARE, not sit at a fixed penalty for some fixed number of days after the
  fact. Same vanilla pattern RUT_VorrelEuphoriaThought already uses in this
  repo (RimWorld/ThoughtWorker_Hediff.cs, read in full there).

  🔴 STAGE COUNT IS LOAD-BEARING, same warning RUT_VorrelEuphoriaThought's
  own header already carries: ThoughtWorker_Hediff indexes THIS def's stage
  list by the HEDIFF's current stage index (RimWorld/ThoughtWorker_Hediff.cs:
  ActiveAtStage(min(hediff stage, hediff stages-1, thought stages-1))).
  RUT_Tarred has three stages; this has three, same order. Add a stage to
  one and you must add it to the other.

  Mood values deliberately small and all negative — this is squalor, not a
  crisis, and per SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1's own tuning law the biome should
  reward players who tolerate mess rather than punish them hard enough to
  force constant cleaning. INVENTED-BUILD, flagged for live tuning.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RUT_TarredThought</defName>
    <workerClass>ThoughtWorker_Hediff</workerClass>
    <hediff>RUT_Tarred</hediff>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>tracked in tar</label>
        <description>My boots are black with it and it is on everything I touch. It could be worse.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>tar-slicked</label>
        <description>It is in my hair, on my hands, down my collar. I can smell myself from an arm's length.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-5</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>tar-caked</label>
        <description>I am wearing more tar than clothing at this point. Everyone can smell it, including me.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-9</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
